[
  {
    "id": "L-282110275400-000",
    "class": "bug",
    "lesson": "The Python harness implicitly assumed \"binary exists\" == \"binary is up to date\": ensure_capture_tool() only ran `make capture-tool` when the file was missing, never when it was stale relative to the MesenCore.dylib/sources it links. This is a class of build-artifact staleness not tracked by git (scripts/headless_record is in .gitignore, so there is no commit timestamp to compare against, only the local disk mtime). The symptom (SIGABRT from a missing dyld symbol, before any HdPackBuilder code runs) was easy to misdiagnose as a logic bug in HdPackBuilder because AC-3 only reports \"process aborted during recording\", without distinguishing a dynamic-loading failure from a real runtime failure. Avoid: compare the binary's mtime against the .dylib's (or simply always invoke `make capture-tool`, which is idempotent and always relinks because the target matches no file and the Makefile declares no .PHONY) instead of an existence check.",
    "scope": [
      "scripts/validate_palette_variants.py"
    ],
    "status": "blocking-in-review",
    "source": "diagnóstico"
  },
  {
    "id": "L-989ce2c41e3e-000",
    "class": "new-feature",
    "lesson": "Decompose phase failed: max iterations (4) exhausted without proxy APPROVE. The same failure recurred on 2026-08-26 when a multi-phase task was again fed to one run. Avoid: never hand a multi-phase PRD to a single dev-squad run — slice it per phase and settle the phase's ADRs first.",
    "scope": [
      "workflow:decompose"
    ],
    "status": "advisory",
    "source": "post-mortem"
  },
